{
  "id": "self-medication",
  "term": "self-medication",
  "definition": "Self-medication is the idea that a person uses alcohol to reduce distressing symptoms such as intrusive memories and heightened arousal. In this model, the short-term relief can unintentionally strengthen continued use and contribute to dependence.",
